{"name":"Singing in the Rain","hex":"#8e9c98","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"singing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of using the voice to produce musical sounds; vocalizing.","Disclosing information, or giving evidence about another."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Smooth and flowing.","Producing a whistling sound due to the escape of steam."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/singing"},{"term":"rain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Condensed water falling from a cloud.","Any matter moving or falling, usually through air, and especially if liquid or otherwise figuratively identifiable with raindrops."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have rain fall from the sky.","To fall as or like rain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Singing in the Rain (Simple Plan song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Singing in the Rain\" is a song by Canadian rock band Simple Plan from their fifth studio album, Taking One for the Team (2016). On the album, American musical duo Rock City are featured on the track, with an additional verse written by the duo's Timothy and Theron Thomas, however the single version does not include this feature. The solo Simple Plan version of \"Singing in the Rain\" was released to digital retailers on March 25, 2016 as the album's third official single."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singing_in_the_Rain_(Simple_Plan_song)","wikidata":"Q26964773"},{"title":"Singin' in the Rain","blocks":[{"text":"Singin' in the Rain is a 1952 American musical romantic comedy film directed and choreographed by Gene Kelly and Stanley Donen, starring Kelly, Donald O'Connor and Debbie Reynolds, with Jean Hagen, Millard Mitchell, Douglas Fowley, Rita Moreno and Cyd Charisse in supporting roles. It offers a lighthearted depiction of Hollywood in the late 1920s, with the three stars portraying performers caught up in the transition from silent films to \"talkies\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Singin%27_in_the_Rain_%281952_poster%29.jpg/330px-Singin%27_in_the_Rain_%281952_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singin'_in_the_Rain","wikidata":"Q309153"},{"title":"Singing","blocks":[{"text":"Singing is the art of creating music with the voice. It is the oldest form of musical expression, and the human voice can be considered the first musical instrument by some. The definition of singing varies across sources. Some sources define singing as the act of creating musical sounds with the voice. Other common definitions include \"the utterance of words or sounds in tuneful succession\" or \"the production of musical tones by means of the human voice\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Ah_cricket_20122_%287364759010%29.jpg/330px-Ah_cricket_20122_%287364759010%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singing","wikidata":"Q27939"},{"title":"Rain","blocks":[{"text":"Rain or rainfall is a form of atmospheric precipitation composed of droplets of water aerosols that have condensed from atmospheric water vapor and fall by gravity. Depending on the intensity, rain can be described as a drizzle, a shower, a cloudburst or a downpour. It is also often accompanied by other weather phenomena such as strong wind (rainstorm) and lightning (thunderstorm), and may be mixed with hail/ice pellet, snow (sleet) and sandstorm. Rain is a major component of the water cycle and is responsible for depositing most of the fresh water on Earth. It provides water for hydroelectric power plants, crop irrigation, and suitable conditions for many types of ecosystems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg/330px-Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rain","wikidata":"Q7925"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Encina_Drive-in_Ad_-_16_May_1952%2C_Santa_Cruz%2C_CA.jpg/500px-Encina_Drive-in_Ad_-_16_May_1952%2C_Santa_Cruz%2C_CA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Encina_Drive-in_Ad_-_16_May_1952%2C_Santa_Cruz%2C_CA.jpg/500px-Encina_Drive-in_Ad_-_16_May_1952%2C_Santa_Cruz%2C_CA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A drive-in advertisement from 1952","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEncina_Drive-in_Ad_-_16_May_1952%2C_Santa_Cruz%2C_CA.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Singin%27_in_the_Rain_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3256647.jpg/500px-Singin%27_in_the_Rain_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3256647.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Singin%27_in_the_Rain_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3256647.jpg/500px-Singin%27_in_the_Rain_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3256647.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Singin' in the Rain playing at the Palace Theatre in London's West End, December 2012","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASingin'_in_the_Rain_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3256647.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Windsbacher_d.jpg/500px-Windsbacher_d.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Windsbacher_d.jpg/500px-Windsbacher_d.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Boys' choir.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWindsbacher_d.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Hals%2C_Frans_-_Sin